{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/package.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:06:45.502042Z","id":"a3bef21f835c3f2d037b0bdf531fc7da94bafdbe3cf19f8ae063bdba45d54e40","body":{"detail":"beforeAll copies web/dist-sdk into the test app's node_modules (cpSync). npm publishes what `npm pack` selects, which honours `files`, .npmignore and npm's always-excluded names. With no `files` field the two agree today; once the package gains a `files` list or a README or an .npmignore, the test would still pass on files npm leaves out.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"ae66846a8da10415c264042b514383a88cc1183350c242f1b5cc7e9d8becb7d5"},"suggested_fix":"Run `npm pack --pack-destination <tmp>` (or `pnpm pack`) on web/dist-sdk and install the tarball into the test app (e.g. extract it into node_modules/@empathic/clax-sdk).","summary":"The package test installs web/dist-sdk by copying the directory, not by `npm pack`, so it does not check what npm would publish","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","npm","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/package.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:11:00.341172Z","id":"cd05196f1679a274b4c39a388250289f8941137e10c17f3051f90855223085b2","body":{"detail":"web/sdk/package.test.ts:38-47 (beforeAll starts at 38, not 39) runs cpSync(pkgDir, installed, {recursive: true}) at :45. https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/commands/npm-publish: with a `files` field 'only the files specified will be included', .npmignore excludes files, and `npm pack` 'figures out the files to be included'. web/scripts/build-sdk.mjs:55-71 sets no `files` and writes no .npmignore, so the copy and the tarball agree today. Kind (suggestion) fits.","kind":"comment","references":"a3bef21f835c3f2d037b0bdf531fc7da94bafdbe3cf19f8ae063bdba45d54e40","summary":"confirmed: the test installs by cpSync of web/dist-sdk, not from an npm pack tarball","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/package.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:41:01.292834Z","id":"529659940e10c26b81b1a22f0901f2facc7f939a925988ec8eb9ab05bc80c94c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c627b3e3","summary":"beforeAll runs `npm pack --json --offline --ignore-scripts --pack-destination <app>` on web/dist-sdk (the Node toolchain's npm under Bazel, @nodejs//:npm_bin via CLAX_NPM_CLI; the npm on PATH natively), extracts the tarball with tar --strip-components=1 under node_modules/@empathic/clax-sdk, and re-reads package.json from it; every check (README, LICENSE, notices, exports, types, bundle) reads the installed copy. `just web-test` (Bazel): //web:sdk_package, :lint, :typecheck, :unit and :bundle_size PASSED.","supersedes":"a3bef21f835c3f2d037b0bdf531fc7da94bafdbe3cf19f8ae063bdba45d54e40","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/package.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T16:20:16.712990Z","id":"4efc59d98403b3eb3fb2f08d26304cd23e75d766746946c3097b6e4857147c1f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7ab95a721b83785274106b3665f9202d96c4ab39","summary":"beforeAll runs `npm pack --json --offline --ignore-scripts --pack-destination <app>` on web/dist-sdk (the Node toolchain's npm under Bazel, @nodejs//:npm_bin via CLAX_NPM_CLI; the npm on PATH natively), extracts the tarball with tar --strip-components=1 under node_modules/@empathic/clax-sdk, and re-reads package.json from it; every check (README, LICENSE, notices, exports, types, bundle) reads the installed copy. `just web-test` (Bazel): //web:sdk_package, :lint, :typecheck, :unit and :bundle_size PASSED.","supersedes":"529659940e10c26b81b1a22f0901f2facc7f939a925988ec8eb9ab05bc80c94c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/package.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T16:31:04.455546Z","id":"70e101608609827c68e994558360a9ea362bd5c9a92b4bc20c7f89eb58d8797d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:372de904a1b7c8fb9062c9aef918772e4b42c107","summary":"beforeAll runs `npm pack --json --offline --ignore-scripts --pack-destination <app>` on web/dist-sdk (the Node toolchain's npm under Bazel, @nodejs//:npm_bin via CLAX_NPM_CLI; the npm on PATH natively), extracts the tarball with tar --strip-components=1 under node_modules/@empathic/clax-sdk, and re-reads package.json from it; every check (README, LICENSE, notices, exports, types, bundle) reads the installed copy. `just web-test` (Bazel): //web:sdk_package, :lint, :typecheck, :unit and :bundle_size PASSED.","supersedes":"4efc59d98403b3eb3fb2f08d26304cd23e75d766746946c3097b6e4857147c1f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/package.json","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:56:47.896413Z","id":"5a6d159c5a9496b4956d21639f331d5b8d6f31e59c322a122f4f7e9d1ca6d641","body":{"detail":"npm documents `repository.directory` as the directory in a monorepo where the package's package.json lives (https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/configuring-npm/package-json#repository). npmjs.com's repository link and changelog tools (such as Renovate's) follow it. web/sdk/package.json says `web`, while its `homepage` names web/sdk, so the published package points at the AGPL web app's directory.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":26},"content_hash":"4ce3b096bae44ecefe6315fc012686d23ae1b1a529bddaef40814dbad8a40423"},"suggested_fix":"Set `\"directory\": \"web/sdk\"` in web/sdk/package.json and add the expected value to the manifest checks in web/sdk/package.test.ts.","summary":"The manifest gives `repository.directory` as `web`, not the package's own directory, web/sdk","tags":["review","review:pr45-client-split","npm","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/package.json","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:42:08.180158Z","id":"fa48f99024099c196b9cc99a54d963e8df8fee13ab0f240983eabf1a2fa230ee","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:485377da2","summary":"web/sdk/package.json's repository.directory is web/sdk; web/sdk/package.test.ts asserts the published repository object. //web:sdk_package passes (bazelisk test --lockfile_mode=error //web/... //scripts/...: 40 tests pass).","supersedes":"5a6d159c5a9496b4956d21639f331d5b8d6f31e59c322a122f4f7e9d1ca6d641","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/package.json","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:43:12.833826Z","id":"20c35e7ed3af53439be70f8f4ff8cbe24f9c170bbff5d79175c80561bca65e70","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4866de92196fc94f5a2cd3db52c219bb01c5e307","summary":"web/sdk/package.json's repository.directory is web/sdk; web/sdk/package.test.ts asserts the published repository object. //web:sdk_package passes (bazelisk test --lockfile_mode=error //web/... //scripts/...: 40 tests pass).","supersedes":"fa48f99024099c196b9cc99a54d963e8df8fee13ab0f240983eabf1a2fa230ee","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:37:27.481574Z","id":"34e9682eb9817a47d45395faf2e0ae9e9bbc8a4f01af6e0cd4762e117c6c73f6","body":{"detail":"web/sdk/README.md is the package's only documentation on npm. Its overlay example passes no `user`, so the reporter's key and token are not kept (web/sdk/src/reporter.ts ReporterOptions.user) and every page load of every visitor mints a token; docs/feedback.md ('What the token route sees') warns that all mints share the service grant's 1,024 requests per 240 s. Its auth also returns res.json() whatever the status, so a refusal from the backend reaches ReporterClient.current() as an object without `token`, which throws the generic 'auth gave no reporter token' and never carries code invalid_key, so the overlay's drop-the-key-and-retry path (reporter.ts:355-361) cannot run. Its page sends the public key as a bare text body while the backend snippet does not show how to read it. And the README never says where the queue ID, the service grant and the queue's origins come from (docs/feedback.md section 1, the Queues page) or links docs/feedback.md or docs/contract.md, so a reader starting from npm cannot get to a working report.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"dfa89354f520cf83229e4c49e30b523afb235c124d700e6c19068554daf72257"},"suggested_fix":"In the README: pass `user: currentUser.id` in the overlay example; throw an error carrying `code` when the token route is not ok (as docs/feedback.md section 3 does); send `{public_key}` as JSON and show the backend reading it; and add a short 'Before you start' that names the Queues page steps (queue, origins, service grant) with links to docs/feedback.md and docs/contract.md 'Report queue routes' on GitHub.","summary":"The npm README's overlay example omits `user` and drops the auth route's error code, the two things docs/feedback.md says an integration must get right","tags":["review","review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:41:07.378309Z","id":"cb45ed6626cf30cce83d4d3b9268ecce00637edd723da386989f4fd9551063a9","body":{"detail":"web/sdk/README.md:27-35: overlay({instance, queue, auth}) with no `user`; auth posts publicKey as a bare body and `return res.json(); // { token, expires_at }` with no res.ok check. web/sdk/src/reporter.ts:34-45: without `user` the key and token 'last as long as the page', so each page load mints. reporter.ts:355-361 rekeys only when auth throws an error whose code is 'invalid_key'; an error body returned as a value instead reaches reporter.ts:363 and throws Error('auth gave no reporter token'). web/overlay/src/main.ts:114 passes opts.user straight to ReporterClient. `grep -n 'feedback.md\\|contract.md\\|docs/' web/sdk/README.md` prints nothing, and the README never says where the queue ID, origins or service grant come from.","kind":"comment","references":"34e9682eb9817a47d45395faf2e0ae9e9bbc8a4f01af6e0cd4762e117c6c73f6","summary":"confirmed: the README's overlay example passes no user and returns res.json() whatever the status, and links neither guide","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:47:53.438579Z","id":"d6d11a6df7cc5c35c689ab7f1c85ba8b774c6752b83890da4cf03ddb45b83a48","body":{"detail":"Commit \"docs(feedback): name the npm package, its LGPL license and the clients' retries\". web/sdk/README.md: 'Before you start' (the Queues page's queue, origins and service grant), links to docs/feedback.md and docs/contract.md#report-queue-routes on GitHub, the overlay example with `user: currentUser.id` and an auth that throws Object.assign(new Error(...), { code }) when the route is not ok, and a backend route that reads `{ public_key }` from the JSON body and passes invalid_key and limit_reached back with their code and Retry-After. //web:sdk_package passes ('carries its README').","kind":"comment","references":"34e9682eb9817a47d45395faf2e0ae9e9bbc8a4f01af6e0cd4762e117c6c73f6","summary":"fixed: the README's overlay example passes user, sends {public_key} as JSON and throws an error carrying the route's code; it has a Before you start and links both guides","tags":["session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
